        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "68c2dd23-d094-5680-a2f9-c20be8d08b9e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: RedBoot, Airbus A380, JFFS2\n- Companies: Red Hat, Airbus, Delta Air Lines\n- Systems: eCos RTOS, Hardware Abstraction Layer, Das U-Boot, Open Firmware\n- Concepts: bootstrap firmware, embedded systems, bootloaders\n\nFacts:\n- RedBoot is an acronym for Red Hat Embedded Debug and Bootstrap firmware.\n- RedBoot is an open source application that uses the eCos real-time operating system Hardware Abstraction Layer to provide bootstrap firmware for embedded systems.\n- RedBoot is used in product development and in deployed products in the field.\n- RedBoot is used in entertainment systems on Airbus A380 aircraft and Delta Air Lines' Boeing 767 aircraft.\n- The Airbus A380 is a double-deck, wide-body, four-engine jet airliner manufactured by Airbus.\n- JFFS2 is available for bootloaders such as Das U-Boot, Open Firmware, eCos RTOS, and RedBoot.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
